A||||4||MrPAW||4spd trans with 5spd Clutch||||5||
Z||000000||MrPAW||11-04-2001||02:47 PM||||Can a 4spd transmission from an 84 be bolted to an engine with a clutch, pressure plate and flywheel from an 86 5spd?<P>Looking at the design of the pressure plates it appears the throwout bearing from the 5spd would have to be used.  Will it work correctly on the 4spd?||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowCG||11-04-2001||10:23 PM||||I believe the throwout brg. is the main difference.<BR>Hopefully someone else will be able and confirm that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||11-06-2001||12:42 PM||||I concur, based only on looking at Centerforce's online catalog.  The disc and pressure plate assemblies they sell for Fiero are the same for 4-sp and 5-sp; but the T/O bearings are different part numbers.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Msaby||11-06-2001||05:01 PM||||do you know what the part numbers are?  manufacture? i am getting ready to do a swap from a 4sp to a 5sp?  <BR>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPAW||11-06-2001||11:30 PM||||I pulled the flywheel / clutch / pressure plate assemblies off both the 86 and the 84 engines and took some measurements.<P>84 4spd Clutch ~ 9 3/16 o.d. 1 1/2 Wide friction surface<P>86 5spd Clutch ~ 8 9/16 o.d. 1 1/4" Wide friction surface<P>These dimensions should not be a problem since I am want to use the matched assembly from the 86. (the 84 assembly is completely trashed - metal to metal, the 86 is like new)<P>The two parts the worry me are:<P>1. The stacked height from the back of the flywheel to the front of the pressure plate is about 1/8" shorter for the 86 assembly. Because of this I am worried that the throwout bearing could run out of travel before completely releasing the clutch.  This could be made up for in the design of the bearing or maybe there is enough travel in the fork to make it insignificant? I'm not sure.<P>2. The way the bearing contacts the finger springs on the pressure plate appears to be different. The 84 appears to use a flat face throwout bearing and the 86 uses a bearing that contacts at one point.  This makes me think I have to use the throwout from the 86 for everything to operate correctly. I am not sure this bearing will work with the 84 4spd clutch fork and sleeve on the input shaft.<P>The 4spd is coming out this weekend and maybe then it will all be obvious.<P>I would hate to get everthing back together, find out that I missed something, it doesn't work right and end up dropping the cradle again!!<P>Thanks,<BR>Paul ||||reg||1
